HeightScale and ForwardHeight use the renamed namespace. LowProfile extracts
and extends the negative-MGF/lower-tail argument, using this project's verified
maximum-height observable. No live sibling-project dependency is used.

The explicit finite product of independent Bernoulli variables was adapted
from Freezing1/BernoulliProductLaw.lean, source SHA-256
832e2960320fd805e3e812be8e347029c13c5388a84c8a891a11b3ab6fd17f92.
The reciprocal-parameter positivity argument was adapted from
Freezing1/ScheduleBernoulli.lean, source SHA-256
a41c4b00d5c31304cfc12ebcffdc3ec63d19d39ee450e1f9dc9ae9634bf2c21f.
Only that finite parameter argument is reused: this project's parameters retain
the reciprocal population at every step and sum only attachment coordinates.
ActiveHeightBernoulli supplies a new proof connecting the actual forward
active-height law to the independent product sum. These sources retain the
companion project's Apache-2.0 attribution above.

The unconditional MGF-to-Bennett-tail lemma in MGFConcentration.lean was
adapted from Freezing1/MGFLimits.lean, source SHA-256
d032302835691d582a427ae5bb8dae286fda760fdb0db7a6b363c3a4f9344c92.
Only that analytic implication is reused, with this project's Bennett rate;
none of the companion's later limit hypotheses is imported. RRTUniformDepth
proves the pure-attachment sampling and normalization bridges in this project.

